<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Jessica Cellitti — Projects</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..40,300;0,9..40,400;0,9..40,500;0,9..40,600;0,9..40,700;1,9..40,300;1,9..40,400&family=DM+Serif+Display:ital@0;1&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

:root {
  --black: #111;
  --gray: #555;
  --gray-light: #888;
  --light: #f5f5f3;
  --border: #e8e8e6;
  --white: #fff;
}

html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }

body {
  font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
  background: var(--white);
  color: var(--black);
  min-height: 100vh;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

/* ── NAV ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
nav {
  position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; z-index: 100;
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.92);
  backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  height: 64px;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
  padding: 0 48px;
}

.nav-logo {
  font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
  font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--black);
  text-decoration: none; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
}

.nav-back {
  font-size: 13px; color: var(--gray); text-decoration: none;
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
  transition: color 0.2s;
}
.nav-back:hover { color: var(--black); }

/* ── HERO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.hero {
  padding: 140px 48px 80px;
  max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.hero-label {
  font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--gray-light); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 20px;
  font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
}

.hero-h1 {
  font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif;
  font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
  line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 20px;
  font-weight: 400;
}

.hero-h1 em {
  font-style: italic; color: var(--gray);
}

.hero-sub {
  font-size: 18px; color: var(--gray); line-height: 1.7;
  max-width: 560px; font-weight: 300;
}

.hero-note {
  font-size: 14px; color: var(--gray-light); line-height: 1.7;
  max-width: 560px; font-weight: 300; margin-top: 20px;
  padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
}

/* ── PROJECTS GRID ───────────────────────────────────────── */
.projects-section {
  padding: 80px 48px 120px;
  max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto;
}


.section-label {
  font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--gray); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;
}

.section-note {
  font-size: 14px; color: var(--gray); font-weight: 300;
  line-height: 1.7; max-width: 620px;
  margin-bottom: 32px; padding-bottom: 20px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.section-label.solo {
  margin-bottom: 40px; padding-bottom: 16px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.projects-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(320px, 1fr));
  gap: 2px;
}

/* ── PROJECT CARD ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
.project-card {
  background: var(--white);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  padding: 36px;
  text-decoration: none;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column;
  transition: all 0.25s ease;
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.project-card::after {
  content: '';
  position: absolute; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
  height: 2px; background: var(--black);
  transform: scaleX(0); transform-origin: left;
  transition: transform 0.3s ease;
}

.project-card:hover { background: var(--light); }
.project-card:hover::after { transform: scaleX(1); }

.card-top {
  display: flex; align-items: flex-start;
  justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 24px;
  gap: 12px;
}

.card-company-logo {
  height: 22px; width: auto;
  filter: grayscale(1) brightness(0);
  opacity: 0.7;
}

.card-company-name {
  font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  color: var(--black); opacity: 0.7; line-height: 22px;
}

.card-type {
  font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--gray); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
  background: var(--light); border: 1px solid var(--border);
  padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 20px; white-space: nowrap;
}

.card-title {
  font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif;
  font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--black);
  margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
}

.card-desc {
  font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--gray);
  margin-bottom: 16px; font-weight: 300;
}

.card-notice {
  font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--gray);
  margin-bottom: 28px; flex: 1; font-weight: 300;
  padding-left: 14px; border-left: 2px solid var(--border);
}
.card-notice strong {
  font-weight: 600; color: var(--black);
  display: block; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 5px;
}

.card-footer {
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 12px;
}

.card-tags {
  display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.card-tag {
  font-size: 11px; color: var(--gray);
  padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px;
  background: var(--border);
}

.card-tag.live {
  background: var(--black); color: var(--white);
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px;
}
.card-tag.live::before {
  content: ''; width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--white); opacity: 0.9;
}

.card-arrow {
  font-size: 18px; color: var(--black);
  transition: transform 0.2s;
}
.project-card:hover .card-arrow { transform: translate(3px, -3px); }


.project-card.coins { cursor: default; }
.project-card.coins:hover { background: var(--white); }
.project-card.coins::after { display: none; }

.coins-links {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px;
  margin-top: auto; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 4px;
}
.coins-links a {
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
  font-size: 14px; color: var(--black); text-decoration: none;
  padding: 11px 0 11px 0; font-weight: 400;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  transition: padding-left 0.2s, color 0.2s;
}
.coins-links a:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.coins-links a span { color: var(--gray-light); font-size: 15px; transition: transform 0.2s; }
.coins-links a:hover { padding-left: 6px; }
.coins-links a:hover span { color: var(--black); transform: translate(3px, -3px); }

/* ── RESPONSIVE ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  nav { padding: 0 24px; }
  .hero { padding: 100px 24px 60px; }
  .projects-section { padding: 48px 24px 80px; }
  .projects-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .project-card { padding: 28px; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<nav>
  <a class="nav-logo" href="https://www.jessicacellitti.com">Jessica Cellitti</a>
  <a class="nav-back" href="https://www.jessicacellitti.com">← Back to portfolio</a>
</nav>

<main>
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-label">Projects</div>
    <h1 class="hero-h1">Work samples &amp; <em>applied projects</em></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">Hands-on deliverables built for real job applications. Each project reflects how I approach learning design, customer education, and learning strategy for specific companies and roles.</p>
    <p class="hero-note">Several of these were built for a specific opening, using that company's real product and whatever was publicly documented about it. Where a project makes claims about a company I don't have inside access to, it says so on the page.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="projects-section">
    <div class="section-label solo">All projects</div>
    <div class="projects-grid">

      <!-- AI FLUENCY -->
      <a class="project-card" href="/ai-fluency">
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-company-name">Anthropic</span>
          <span class="card-type">Adaptive Program</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card-title">AI Fluency — Personalized Learning Program</div>
        <div class="card-desc">A twenty-minute program that assembles itself around who the learner is — nurse, teacher, or small business owner — and teaches AI collaboration through decisions rather than definitions. Built on Anthropic's open-licensed AI Fluency framework for their AI Fluency Education Lead role.</div>
        <div class="card-notice"><strong>What to notice</strong>Nothing is scored. The debrief has an instructor view that reads the same session as evidence about the course rather than the person — measurement without a knowledge check.</div>
        <div class="card-footer">
          <div class="card-tags">
            <span class="card-tag live">Interactive</span>
            <span class="card-tag">AI Literacy</span>
            <span class="card-tag">Assessment</span>
          </div>
          <span class="card-arrow">↗</span>
        </div>
      </a>

      <!-- FLUX -->
      <a class="project-card" href="/flux">
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-company-name">Flux</span>
          <span class="card-type">Knowledge Infrastructure</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card-title">Flux — Content That Outruns Its Own Maintenance</div>
        <div class="card-desc">Knowledge infrastructure for a fictional AI code-review company shipping multiple releases a month with a one-person learning team. Built for anyone drowning in content that goes stale faster than they can maintain it.</div>
        <div class="card-notice"><strong>What to notice</strong>The live release simulation — watch a single update ripple through content blocks, tickets, and a freshness dashboard in real time. Proof this isn't a static mockup.</div>
        <div class="card-footer">
          <div class="card-tags">
            <span class="card-tag live">Interactive</span>
            <span class="card-tag">Content Ops</span>
            <span class="card-tag">Systems</span>
          </div>
          <span class="card-arrow">↗</span>
        </div>
      </a>

      <!-- TRUNK TOOLS -->
      <a class="project-card" href="/trunk-tools-track">
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-company-name">Trunk Tools</span>
          <span class="card-type">Certification Track</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card-title">TrunkSubmittal Certification Track</div>
        <div class="card-desc">One certification module built end-to-end for Trunk Tools' real AI-Enabled GC product — storyboard, sample assessment, live-session rubric, and a certification tracker. Built for their Instructional Designer &amp; Learning Operations Lead opening, grounded in their actual product mechanism and a public customer deployment.</div>
        <div class="card-notice"><strong>What to notice</strong>The deliberately incorrect flag baked into the assessment — the certification tests judgment, not compliance with whatever the tool returns.</div>
        <div class="card-footer">
          <div class="card-tags">
            <span class="card-tag">Construction Tech</span>
            <span class="card-tag">Certification</span>
          </div>
          <span class="card-arrow">↗</span>
        </div>
      </a>

      <!-- THE SCORE -->
      <a class="project-card" href="/the-score">
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-company-name">Conductor</span>
          <span class="card-type">Content Audit</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card-title">The Score — Content Health Dashboard</div>
        <div class="card-desc">A content-health dashboard modeled on Conductor, a real SEO and content platform, built entirely from what's publicly visible about their content ecosystem — no login access. A first-pass illustration of what a content audit and lifecycle-coverage system could look like for them.</div>
        <div class="card-notice"><strong>What to notice</strong>It's explicitly labeled as illustrative and dated — an honest account of what could be inferred from the outside versus what would need real access to confirm.</div>
        <div class="card-footer">
          <div class="card-tags">
            <span class="card-tag live">Interactive</span>
            <span class="card-tag">Content Strategy</span>
            <span class="card-tag">SEO</span>
          </div>
          <span class="card-arrow">↗</span>
        </div>
      </a>

      <!-- RAIN -->
      <a class="project-card" href="/rain-onboarding">
        <div class="card-top">
          <img class="card-company-logo" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Rain">
          <span class="card-type">Onboarding Course</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card-title">Rain — CX Onboarding Course</div>
        <div class="card-desc">A seven-module interactive course built for Rain's customer experience team. Covers stablecoin infrastructure, card programs, partner use cases, and CX essentials.</div>
        <div class="card-notice"><strong>What to notice</strong>AI-powered reflection feedback — learners write a response and get a reply that reacts to what they actually said.</div>
        <div class="card-footer">
          <div class="card-tags">
            <span class="card-tag live">Interactive</span>
            <span class="card-tag">Fintech</span>
            <span class="card-tag">CX</span>
          </div>
          <span class="card-arrow">↗</span>
        </div>
      </a>

      <!-- COINS -->
      <div class="project-card coins">
        <div class="card-top">
          <span class="card-company-name">COINS</span>
          <span class="card-type">Three-Part System</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card-title">COINS CX — Learning System</div>
        <div class="card-desc">One fictional stablecoin fintech approached three ways: the strategy that defines the system, the interface a learner meets it through, and the onboarding course inside it. Covers onboarding through T4 specialist certification, a QA-driven content loop, and BPO-partner enablement.</div>
        <div class="card-notice"><strong>What to notice</strong>The QA loop's escalation-quality example — a genuine diagnose-before-build methodology, not a content calendar. And the same problem held at three altitudes.</div>
        <div class="coins-links">
          <a href="/coins-learning-strategy">Learning strategy <span>&#8599;</span></a>
          <a href="/coins-lms">LMS design mockup <span>&#8599;</span></a>
          <a href="/coins-onboarding">Onboarding course <span>&#8599;</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

</main>

</body>
</html>
